# Walkthrough - Chat Real-time Updates

I have implemented a polling mechanism to ensure the chat interface updates automatically when new messages arrive.

## Changes

### 1. Polling Logic in [MessageList](file:///d:/Workshop/line_oa/admin_panel/src/components/chat/message-list.tsx#34-104)

I modified [src/components/chat/message-list.tsx](file:///d:/Workshop/line_oa/admin_panel/src/components/chat/message-list.tsx) to:
- Use `useState` to manage the message list state.
- Use `useEffect` with `setInterval` to fetch new messages every 3 seconds using the [getMessages](file:///d:/Workshop/line_oa/admin_panel/src/actions/chat.actions.ts#40-59) server action.
- Update the UI only when new messages are detected.

### 2. Passing `customerId`

I updated [src/app/(dashboard)/chat/[customerId]/page.tsx](file:///d:/Workshop/line_oa/admin_panel/src/app/%28dashboard%29/chat/%5BcustomerId%5D/page.tsx) to pass the `customerId` prop to the [MessageList](file:///d:/Workshop/line_oa/admin_panel/src/components/chat/message-list.tsx#34-104) component, which is required for the polling function to know which conversation to fetch.

## Verification Results

### Manual Verification
- [x] Verified that the chat page loads correctly with initial messages.
- [x] Verified that the polling mechanism triggers every 3 seconds (code review).
- [x] Confirmed that [getMessages](file:///d:/Workshop/line_oa/admin_panel/src/actions/chat.actions.ts#40-59) is called with the correct `customerId`.

## Next Steps
- Monitor the performance impact of polling.
- Consider moving to Websockets or Server-Sent Events (SSE) in the future for even faster updates and lower server load if the user base grows significantly.
